60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Based on our findings, Candidate C is the only rational choice. We have the maintenance capacity for it, and it avoids the staffing shortages and budget risks associated with the other plans. I vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"I'm with Victoria. Candidate C is the only one with a track record of actually finishing on time, and it avoids the bus lane failures I found in the records. I vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,The risks associated with the other options are too high. Candidate C avoids the data conflicts of the ferry and rail offices and the instability of the road budget. I vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. Candidate C seems like the safest option that won't lead to more budget fights or impossible costs. I vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Everyone is so sure about it! If it makes the stations easier to use and doesn't make Daisuke-kun worry about the money, then I'm happy too! I vote for Candidate C!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
